  "worked_solution": "The product rule for derivatives gives\n\n$$\n{p}^{\u2032}(x)={f}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot h(x)+f(x)\\cdot {h}^{\u2032}(x).\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{p}^{\u2032}(2)={f}^{\u2032}(2)\\cdot h(2)+f(2)\\cdot {h}^{\u2032}(2).\n$$\n\nFrom the graphs above, we obtain that $f(2)=1$ and $h(2)=-1.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n- The slope of $f(x)$ on $x\\in (1,3)$ equals $-1.$ So, ${f}^{\u2032}(2)=-1.$\n\n- The slope of $h(x)$ on $x\\in (1,3)$ equals $-2.$ So, ${h}^{\u2032}(2)=-2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{\u2032}(2) & ={f}^{\u2032}(2)\\cdot h(2)+f(2)\\cdot {h}^{\u2032}(2) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
